    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's what I changed:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `customerCode` format changed from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to **`<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`** with a per-city sequence.\n\n**1. `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the generator:\n- Added `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of `city`.\n- Changed `NNNN` from a *global* owner count to a *per-city* count (owners already in that city + 1), computed by filtering `findAll()` on matching city.\n- Format string is now `\"%s-%s-%04d\"`, producing e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007`.\n- Updated the Javadoc accordingly.\n\n**2. `OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 no code change needed. The `membershipNumber` derivation (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) reads `getCustomerCode()` at mapping time, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`). It is the only value derived from `customerCode` (`membershipTier` derives from `namesakeCount`/`email`, not the code).\n\n**3. `openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` descriptions/examples to match the new format so the API docs stay accurate.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (which asserts the regex `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) now passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.",
